# Node sizes its heap from the machine's RAM. On a laptop with modest RAM a
# full `electron-vite build` can hit the ceiling and die with "Ineffective
# mark-compacts near heap limit" — Monaco and shiki make the renderer bundle
# heavy (monaco-setup alone is ~7 MB).
#
# npm injects this as NODE_OPTIONS into anything it spawns, npx included.
# It raises the ceiling; it does not reserve the memory.
#
# NOTE: this does NOT cover CI. The release workflow's build jobs don't check
# the repo out — they consume the `decrypted-source` artifact, and
# actions/upload-artifact excludes hidden files, so no dotfile in this repo
# ever reaches a build runner. CI gets the same ceiling from NODE_OPTIONS in
# .github/workflows/release.yml, which has to be kept in sync with this.
node-options=--max-old-space-size=4096
